# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) to run the game against a Supabase backend.
# Leave every value empty, or have no .env.local at all, and the game is the
# local hotseat client with no sign-in, exactly as before. See docs/deploy.md.
#
# Both values are public by design (row-level security guards the data).
# Never put a secret, service-role or database key in a VITE_ variable: Vite
# bakes every VITE_ variable into the JavaScript it ships.

# Local Supabase (`npx supabase start` prints both): the API URL, usually
# http://127.0.0.1:54321, and the anon / publishable key.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# On Vercel nothing needs setting by hand: the Supabase Marketplace integration
# injects NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL and NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY,
# which the client reads too, and SUPABASE_URL / SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY for /api.

# Preview deployments (#107) talk to their pull request's Supabase branch. Set
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PRODUCTION_URL in Vercel (Preview and Production) to
# production's Supabase URL: a preview handed that URL then refuses it.
# Unset, previews run unguarded and say so ("guard not configured"). Not
# needed locally. See "Preview branches" in docs/deploy.md.
